					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <div class="image-container floatright"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/k-class-complete-list/k-class2.png" width="305px" alt="k-class2.png" class="image" /></div> <p>K-Class Scenarios are hypothetical situations that could have drastic effects on normality or reality, including the <em>end of the world</em>. The Foundation games out what can happen in these events, and authors on the wiki often reference these contingency plans&#8230; or times they have failed.</p> <p>This collaborative page exists to document all K-Class Scenarios used on the wiki.</p> <p><strong>Disclaimers</strong></p> <ul> <li>There is no canon definition for <em>any</em> K-Class Scenario. This page should <em>not</em> be seen as a &quot;canonical&quot; resource. Please do not hassle authors for &quot;misusing&quot; these scenarios.</li> <li>This list is meant to be <em>descriptive</em>, not <em>prescriptive</em>. Definitions are based on usage in articles, not what anyone <em>thinks</em> they <em>should</em> mean. (For earlier lists with invented definitions, scroll down.)</li> </ul> <p><strong>A bit on notation:</strong> (I treated any of these grammatical variants as equivalent.)</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <ul> <li>Scenarios <em>generally</em> follow: &lt;Letter&gt;K-Class &lt;description/end-of-the-world&gt; scenario</li> <li>&quot;K-class <em>scenario</em>&quot; and &quot;K-class <em>event</em>&quot; seem to be used interchangeably. There's no consistent logic to it. Scenario was used about 4 times as often as event in my initial search.</li> <li>Capitalization (XK-Class End&#8230;, XK-class end&#8230;) and truncation (end-of-the-world, &quot;end of the world&quot;, end of the world) don't seem to have any set standard.</li> </ul> </div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> </div> </div> <p><strong>Do you want to help?</strong><br /> Please do! This is a collaboration. See the steps below:</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;So&nbsp;you&nbsp;want&nbsp;to&nbsp;link&nbsp;an&nbsp;article?</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>So you want to link an article?</strong></p> <ul> <li>Please, please do this! My initial scraping only covered <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/k-class-scenario">tagged</a> SCPs, so tales and other articles need attention.</li> <li>Make sure the article is staying in the positive ratings (remaining at +1 or above for 24 hours) before adding the link: it's a pain to go through and clean up afterwards.</li> <li>If the article uses an existing prefix and fits a common definition, just add the link and update the count (# SCPs, # Tales, # Others). Maybe add the Alternative title if it's new and sounds cool.</li> <li>If the scenario is inconsistent with others in that prefix, OR is the first article using a prefix, OR only appears in a -J, please add it to the appropriate table using this format:</li> </ul> <div class="code"> <pre> <code>||~ Title ||~ Definition ||~ Articles || || || || ||</code> </pre></div> <ul> <li>If you need a whole tab, here is a basic format:</li> </ul> <div class="code"> <pre> <code>[[tab prefix]] **Most Common:** **Used in:** # SCPs, # Tales, # Other **Primary definition:** **Alternative titles:** **SCPs:** **Tales and other articles:** **Inconsistent Uses** ||~ Title ||~ Definition ||~ Articles || || || || || [[/tab]]</code> </pre></div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;So&nbsp;you&nbsp;want&nbsp;to&nbsp;add&nbsp;or&nbsp;update&nbsp;a&nbsp;definition?</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>So you want to add or update a definition?</strong><br /> Maybe you were the author of a one-off or inconsistent-use scenario, or maybe you want to update a primary definition that is out of date. (Or, you know, if it could be better.) Go for it! Just remember:</p> <ul> <li>Definitions should be <em>usage</em>-based. Only create or update definitions to fit their use in articles.</li> <li>If the usage and title is really different from its current prefix, consider adding it to &quot;Inconsistent Uses&quot;.</li> <li>It helps if you add a note down in the &quot;Short description of changes:&quot; before you hit &quot;Save&quot;</li> <li>Do not add definitions without a successful, linked article!</li> </ul> </div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <div id="wiki-tabview-00a5a81df986d0286a654d04ff4fc77b" class="yui-navset"> <ul class="yui-nav"> <li class="selected"><a href="javascript:;"><em>Scenarios With Multiple Uses</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>AK*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>ADK</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>CK©</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>EK*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>GK/GH©</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>HK*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>IK*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>LK*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>MK*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>NK©</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>PK</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>QK</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>RK*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>SK©</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>TK</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>UK</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>VK</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>WK</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>XK©</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>YK*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>ZK©</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Lifted Veil*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>AE</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>BI</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>K</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Missing?</em></a></li> </ul> <div class="yui-content"> <div id="wiki-tab-0-0"> <p>Each of these letter combinations have been used at least twice on the wiki. They are presented alphabetically by K-Class followed by non-K designations and oddities. (GH gets to be special by seniority).</p> <p>For one-off scenarios and versions seen only in -Js, scroll down.</p> <p>Scenarios with *'s have appeared at least 5 times with a consistent definition.<br /> Scenarios with ©'s have appeared at least 10 times with a consistent definition, and could be considered &quot;well-established.&quot; <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Also you have to pay me 5¢ to use them.</span></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-1" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Most Common: AK-class end-of-the-world scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 7 SCPs, 1 Tales, # Other<br /> <strong>Primary definition:</strong> Related to a memetically spread behavior or &quot;madness.&quot; Could be apocalyptic (e.g., people prioritize the behavior over eating/survival) or just radically reorient society around the behavior.</p> <p>Some of these links just say &quot;AK-class end of the world&quot; without defining it.<br /> <strong>Alternative titles:</strong> AK-class &quot;madness&quot; end of the world scenario</p> <p><strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1101">SCP-1101</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3443">SCP-3443</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-571">SCP-571</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1985">SCP-1985</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3060">SCP-3060</a>, <a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-1118-ru">SCP-1118-RU</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4547">SCP-4547</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/reboot-or-how-i-learned-to-stop-worrying-and-love-the-apocal">Reboot or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love the Apocalypses</a></p> <strong>Inconsistent Uses</strong><br /> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Title</th> <th>Definition</th> <th>Articles</th> </tr> <tr> <td>AK-class scenario (Agricultural breakdown)</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1623">SCP-1623</a></td> </tr> </table> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-2" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Most Common: ADK-Class &quot;Complete Anomalous Destabilization&quot; Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 1 SCP, 1 Tale, 0 Other<br /> <strong>Primary definition:</strong> A general scenario which occurs when the &quot;anomalous&quot; reclaims the Earth. Typically occurs 1 to 3 years after an unspecified human extinction event or SK-Class Dominance Shift.<br /> <strong>Alternative titles:</strong> N/A</p> <p><strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3309">SCP-3309</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/umbral-migratory-sequence">UMBRAL_MIGRATORY_SEQUENCE.txt</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-3" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Most Common: CK-Class Restructuring Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 43 SCPs, 12 Tales, # Other<br /> <strong>Primary definition:</strong> Reality is changed by a deity/reality bender/retrocausal altering of history/etc. These can be radical, broad changes representing a true end of the world, or small &quot;localized&quot; changes. (See also RK)<br /> <strong>Alternative titles:</strong> CK-class Reality Restructuring Scenario, CK-class reality-ending scenario, CK-Class Reconfiguration event, CK-class restructuring of modern society, CK-Class (&quot;End-of-Reality&quot;) Scenario</p> <p><strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1012">SCP-1012</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1237">SCP-1237</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-140">SCP-140</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1425">SCP-1425</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-179">SCP-179</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1968">SCP-1968</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1985">SCP-1985</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2046">SCP-2046</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2047">SCP-2047</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2311">SCP-2311</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2330">SCP-2330</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2743">SCP-2743</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2901">SCP-2901</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2975">SCP-2975</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3188">SCP-3188</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3189">SCP-3189</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3391">SCP-3391</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3426">SCP-3426</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3480">SCP-3480</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3498">SCP-3498</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3557">SCP-3557</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3600">SCP-3600</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3648">SCP-3648</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3672">SCP-3672</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3739">SCP-3739</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3742">SCP-3742</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3797">SCP-3797</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3919">SCP-3919</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3936">SCP-3936</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3999">SCP-3999</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4001">SCP-4001</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4010">SCP-4010</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4121">SCP-4121</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4255">SCP-4255</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4260">SCP-4260</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4656">SCP-4656</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-591">SCP-591</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/wmdd-s-proposal">WMDD's Proposal</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/wrong-proposal">Wrong Proposal</a>, <a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-cn-166">SCP-CN-166</a>, <a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-1961-ru">SCP-1961-RU</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5500">SCP-5500</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-beast-beneath-the-library">The Beast Beneath The Library</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/dandelions">Of Multiverses and Dandelion Wine</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/dressing-up">Girls' Night Out: Dressing Up</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/incident-239-b-clef-kondraki">Incident 239-B - Clef-Kondraki</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/incident-zero-part-2">Incident Zero - Part 2</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/incident-zero-part-3">Incident Zero - Part 3</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/memetics-and-infohazards-division-orientation">Memetics and Infohazards Division Orientation</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/persephone-project">Persephone Project</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/recovered-data-file">Recovered Data File</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/sh-tpost-and-c-plastics-tale">Fools of Us All</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/this-is-the-real-life">It's All True</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/what-i-do-for-myself">Changes All That Is Around Me</a></p> <strong>Inconsistent Uses</strong><br /> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Title</th> <th>Definition</th> <th>Articles</th> </tr> <tr> <td>CK-Class &quot;Freaky Friday&quot; scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/mzl-1730">MZL-1730</a></td> </tr> </table> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-4" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Most Common: EK-Class End of Human Consciousness</strong><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 6 SCPs, 2 Tales, 1 Other<br /> <strong>Primary definition:</strong> Total loss of human consciousness. Sometimes just obliviated due to complete memetic replacement or corruption. (See also MK, ED-K)<br /> <strong>Alternative titles:</strong> N/A</p> <p><strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1427">SCP-1427</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1985">SCP-1985</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2007">SCP-2007</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-338">SCP-338</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3498">SCP-3498</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4741">SCP-4741</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/stage-fright">Stage Fright</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/richardson-island">Richardson Island</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/self-similar">Self.Similar.</a></p> <strong>Inconsistent Uses</strong><br /> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Title</th> <th>Definition</th> <th>Articles</th> </tr> <tr> <td>EK-class Foundation collapse scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2807">SCP-2807</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>EK-Class erasure scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4104">SCP-4104</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>EK-Class Evolutionary Restructuring Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3069">SCP-3069</a></td> </tr> </table> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-5" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Most Common: GH-0 'Dead Greenhouse' scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 10 SCPs, 1 Tales, 1 Other<br /> <strong>Primary definition:</strong> Originally appearing in the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/document-recovered-from-the-marianas-trench">Marianas Trench document</a>, where it meant that humans are endangered/extinct but Earth is still fit for habitation. Usage of G-Class scenarios in SCPs is inconsistent but usually involves habitability.<br /> <strong>Alternative titles:</strong> GH-Class &quot;Dead Greenhouse&quot; event, GK-Class End of the World Scenario, GK-class hostile-greenhouse scenario, GK Class Climate Inversion event, GH-Class &quot;Colorless Plague&quot; end-of-humanity event, GK-Class &quot;Broken Greenhouse&quot;</p> <p><strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-540">SCP-540</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1751">SCP-1751</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2029">SCP-2029</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2543">SCP-2543</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2554">SCP-2554</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2702">SCP-2702</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4237">SCP-4237</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4547">SCP-4547</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4568">SCP-4568</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5055">SCP-5055</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/document-recovered-from-the-marianas-trench">Document Recovered from the Marianas Trench</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2305-collab">SCP-2305-A Extended Documentation Log</a></p> <strong>Inconsistent Uses</strong><br /> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Title</th> <th>Definition</th> <th>Articles</th> </tr> <tr> <td>Evento de Antigravedad Global 